Body:
Why is this still unresolved?

This is a serious cost issue for anyone using Claude through third-party Anthropic-compatible providers. Without a stable `metadata.user_id`, prompt caching may silently fail: `cache_creation_input_tokens` keeps increasing, while `cache_read_input_tokens` remains 0. In practice this can make usage cost more than 10x higher.

I verified the workaround described here. A small local proxy that injects the following field into the request body fixes the problem immediately:

{
  "metadata": {
    "user_id": "xxx"
  }
}

After adding a stable `metadata.user_id`, cache reads started working again.

Please add an official config option to pass through or generate a stable `metadata.user_id` for Anthropic-compatible providers. This should not require every user to run a local proxy to avoid massive unexpected costs.
